WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.730
It's been a long time since Peter Jackson
dazzled moviegoers with his award-winning,

00:00:04.730 --> 00:00:07.529
blockbuster trilogy adaptation of J.R.R.

00:00:07.529 --> 00:00:09.000
Tolkien's The Lord of the Rings.

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.910
And although Jackson followed that up with
his Hobbit series, the stars behind Frodo's

00:00:12.910 --> 00:00:18.110
quest to take the ring to Mordor have changed
quite a bit since the original LOTR films.

00:00:18.110 --> 00:00:21.490
Here's what the people of Middle Earth have
been up to since the one ring to rule them

00:00:21.490 --> 00:00:23.830
all was tossed into the fire.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:25.240
Elijah Wood

00:00:25.240 --> 00:00:29.140
Before he became Frodo Baggins, Elijah Wood
was a well-known child star who'd appeared

00:00:29.140 --> 00:00:32.160
in movies like Radio Flyer and The Good Son.

00:00:32.160 --> 00:00:36.110
But Lord of the Rings helped to jettison the
actor into the full-on mainstream.

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:40.620
After that, he started nabbing roles in films
like Sin City and Eternal Sunshine of the

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:41.690
Spotless Mind.

00:00:41.690 --> 00:00:46.000
In addition to returning for The Hobbit in
2012, he's also continued to star on the big

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.710
screen as well as television.

00:00:47.710 --> 00:00:53.260
He recently appeared in BBC America's Dirk
Gently's Holistic Detective Agency and stars

00:00:53.260 --> 00:00:56.300
in Netflix's I Don't Feel at Home in this
World Anymore.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:57.300
"We're badasses now.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.070
We're big badasses..."

00:00:59.070 --> 00:01:00.330
Sean Astin

00:01:00.330 --> 00:01:05.030
Perhaps best known for his role as Frodo's
right-hand man, Samwise Gamgee, actor Sean

00:01:05.030 --> 00:01:08.289
Astin no longer looks like the Hobbit who
made him famous.

00:01:08.289 --> 00:01:12.210
Like Elijah Wood, Astin was also known for
the roles he played as a young man — in

00:01:12.210 --> 00:01:16.719
films like The Goonies and Rudy — long before
he ever set foot in the Shire.

00:01:16.719 --> 00:01:20.380
However, his post-Lord of the Rings career
is a little less busy.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:24.520
He's landed a few small roles in movies and
television series, but nothing's managed to

00:01:24.520 --> 00:01:25.819
stick just yet.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:30.119
He may enjoy a career turnaround, though,
after appearing in the much-anticipated second

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:33.049
season of Netflix's Stranger Things.

00:01:33.049 --> 00:01:34.439
Ian McKellen

00:01:34.439 --> 00:01:39.049
Inarguably the most decorated of all the Lord
of the Rings cast members, Sir Ian McKellen

00:01:39.049 --> 00:01:43.299
looks even wiser now than he did with a staff
in his hand as the wizard Gandalf.

00:01:43.299 --> 00:01:47.649
The actor continued to enjoy his prominent
role in the X-Men movies and most recently

00:01:47.649 --> 00:01:51.999
played Cogsworth in Beauty and the Beast and
the title role of King Lear on-stage.

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.660
He also remains one of the staunchest and
most influential advocates for LGBT rights.

00:01:58.280 --> 00:01:59.840
Sean Bean

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:04.499
Whether or not you had sympathy for Boromir,
Sean Bean's next high fantasy character would

00:02:04.499 --> 00:02:10.259
suffer a fate that broke the hearts of millions
and informed an entire series of family vengeance.

00:02:10.259 --> 00:02:14.810
Although Bean has also enjoyed roles in major
movies like Troy, National Treasure, and The

00:02:14.810 --> 00:02:19.629
Martian, he may be best known these days for
his short-lived turn as Ned Stark on HBO's

00:02:19.629 --> 00:02:20.709
Game of Thrones.

00:02:20.709 --> 00:02:24.920
He's been gone from the show for several seasons,
but his face has not been forgotten by the

00:02:24.920 --> 00:02:25.980
people of Westeros.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:28.450
"Tell them the North remembers."

00:02:28.450 --> 00:02:32.739
Sean Bean has since capitalized on that small
screen attention and nabbed roles in shows

00:02:32.739 --> 00:02:35.750
like Missing, Legends, and Broken.

00:02:35.750 --> 00:02:37.489
Viggo Mortensen

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:41.879
Becoming the King of Gondor was certainly
the big break Viggo Mortensen had been waiting

00:02:41.879 --> 00:02:45.569
for, but it's not his defining role by any
stretch of the imagination.

00:02:45.569 --> 00:02:50.920
The actor has since impressed in films like
A History of Violence, The Road, Eastern Promises,

00:02:50.920 --> 00:02:52.739
and Captain Fantastic.

00:02:52.739 --> 00:02:57.620
And Mortensen has since branched out in artistry
as well, founding a publishing company and

00:02:57.620 --> 00:03:00.480
creating his own poetry books and paintings.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:05.409
He's also known to have rocked out with Buckethead,
producing multiple albums with the avant-garde

00:03:05.409 --> 00:03:06.620
guitarist.

00:03:06.620 --> 00:03:07.849
Orlando Bloom

00:03:07.849 --> 00:03:12.850
After appearing as the elven archer Legolas,
Orlando Bloom earned instant heartthrob status

00:03:12.850 --> 00:03:18.230
and prime placement in several other blockbusters,
including Troy and the Pirates of the Caribbean

00:03:18.230 --> 00:03:19.230
series.

00:03:19.230 --> 00:03:24.300
He also made at least one error in job judgment
by starring in the critically maligned Elizabethtown.

00:03:25.680 --> 00:03:26.860
"Come on."

00:03:26.870 --> 00:03:31.129
Despite that setback, Bloom has continued
to ride the wave of franchises that have informed

00:03:31.129 --> 00:03:35.770
his career over the past two decades by picking
back up his bow for the Hobbit trilogy and

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:38.409
appearing in the latest Pirates pic.

00:03:38.409 --> 00:03:39.969
Liv Tyler

00:03:39.969 --> 00:03:43.879
Also earning heartthrob status in Lord of
the Rings was Arwen, the elven love interest

00:03:43.879 --> 00:03:44.879
of Aragorn.

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:49.250
Nowadays, Liv Tyler has managed to break away
from her fantastic image and status as the

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:53.609
daughter of Aerosmith's Steven Tyler to forge
a career all her own.

00:03:53.609 --> 00:03:58.110
Formerly a teenage model, Tyler got her acting
start in the mid-90s appearing in films like

00:03:58.110 --> 00:04:03.790
Empire Records and Armageddon, and has since
continued to amass an impressive resume, most

00:04:03.790 --> 00:04:08.880
recently appearing in HBO's The Leftovers
as the terrifying cult leader Meg.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:10.379
Dominic Monaghan

00:04:10.379 --> 00:04:14.709
Merry might've been the most serious of the
shire folk, but in real life, Dominic Monaghan

00:04:14.709 --> 00:04:16.560
is about as laid back as they come.

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:21.060
The animal-lover is a vocal advocate for nature,
even earning his own show about tracking down

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:23.590
rare species of animals and insects.

00:04:23.590 --> 00:04:27.050
And even though he was part of the Lord of
the Rings fellowship, he may be better known

00:04:27.050 --> 00:04:30.930
for his heartbreaking work on the small screen
series Lost.

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:32.620
Billy Boyd

00:04:32.620 --> 00:04:36.840
Unlike most of his co-stars, the man who played
Pippin Took in the Lord of the Rings movies

00:04:36.840 --> 00:04:38.710
hasn't become a Hollywood staple.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:42.450
Rather, Billy Boyd is more of a musician than
a thespian these days.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:47.120
He did appear alongside Russell Crowe in Master
and Commander and starred in several indies,

00:04:47.120 --> 00:04:50.210
but he's also the lead singer-guitarist for
a band called Beecake.

00:04:50.210 --> 00:04:55.000
That musical prowess has come full circle
for him, as he wrote and performed the end-credits

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:56.901
theme for The Hobbit: The Battle of the Five
Armies.

00:04:56.901 --> 00:04:57.901
Of course, we probably shouldn't be too surprised
to see him hit the musical scene after his

00:04:57.901 --> 00:04:58.901
stunning solo performance in Return of the
King.

00:04:58.901 --> 00:04:59.901
John Rhys-Davies

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:04.460
In addition to being known for his axe-swinging
skills as the dwarf Gimli, John Rhys-Davies

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:09.099
is also recognizable as the man who starred
as Sallah in the Indiana Jones films.

00:05:09.099 --> 00:05:13.479
Unlike his dwarf counterpart, the actor would
have no trouble seeing over a ledge — because

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:15.620
in real life, he's over six feet tall.

00:05:15.620 --> 00:05:20.520
He can currently be seen in another fantasy
drama series called The Shannara Chronicles.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.360
Hugo Weaving

00:05:22.360 --> 00:05:26.520
Although he might be remembered for his turn
as Lord Elrond in Lord of the Rings, Hugo

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:31.690
Weaving's face is probably even more associated
with The Matrix, since he starred as the inescapable

00:05:31.690 --> 00:05:33.500
Agent Smith in that trilogy as well.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:38.389
He has also enjoyed prime placement in pics
like V for Vendetta, Captain America: The

00:05:38.389 --> 00:05:41.580
First Avenger, and most recently, Hacksaw
Ridge.

00:05:41.580 --> 00:05:46.550
Weaving will also re-team with Peter Jackson
to act in 2018's Mortal Engines.

00:05:46.550 --> 00:05:48.069
Cate Blanchett

00:05:48.069 --> 00:05:52.699
The fabulous actress behind the elven queen
Galadriel needs no introduction.

00:05:52.699 --> 00:05:56.582
Shortly after the Lord of the Rings trilogy
ended, Cate Blanchett won her first of two

00:05:56.582 --> 00:05:59.010
Academy Awards for The Aviator.

00:05:59.010 --> 00:06:02.789
After that, she had no trouble nabbing role
after role on the big screen.

00:06:02.789 --> 00:06:07.889
Notable highlights include Notes on a Scandal,
Hanna, and Blue Jasmine, the film that earned

00:06:07.889 --> 00:06:09.889
her a second Oscar for her shelf.

00:06:09.889 --> 00:06:14.759
She's also joined Hugo Weaving in the Marvel
bad guy club as the villain Hela in Thor:

00:06:14.759 --> 00:06:19.819
Ragnarok, and she's set to appear in the gender-bent
Ocean's Eleven spin-off Ocean's Eight.

00:06:19.819 --> 00:06:21.169
David Wenham

00:06:21.169 --> 00:06:25.940
After becoming Faramir for Lord of the Rings,
David Wenham went on to star in 300 as well

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:28.520
as other films and small screen series.

00:06:28.520 --> 00:06:33.150
Most recently, Wenham starred in BBC's Top
of the Lake and Netflix's Marvel series Iron

00:06:33.150 --> 00:06:37.930
Fist and he's also stepped behind the lens
to make his directorial debut with Ellipsis.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:39.190
Thanks for watching!

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:42.300
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:44.360
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

